  "code": "// T is bounded by Animal, so a T value narrows through Animal with isa\ndescribe[T: Animal](x: T) -> string =>\n    if isa CAT(x) then x.purr()\n    else x.name()\n    fi;",
  "fullSource": "use IO.Std.write_line;\n\nclass Animal abstract is\n    name() -> string;\nsi\n\nclass CAT: Animal is\n    init() is si\n    name() -> string => \"cat\";\n    purr() -> string => \"purr\";\nsi\n\n// T is bounded by Animal, so a T value narrows through Animal with isa\ndescribe[T: Animal](x: T) -> string =>\n    if isa CAT(x) then x.purr()\n    else x.name()\n    fi;\n\nentry() is\n    write_line(describe(CAT()));\nsi\n",
